L2625  
L2626  If I were to suggest anything, it might be to enhance the imagery with a sensory detail --- something that brings the reader closer to the scene, like the warmth of the fries or the hum of the hotel air conditioning. While it doesn’t follow the traditional 5-7-5 syllable pattern, which is perfectly fine for a modern haiku, experimenting with that structure could add a rhythmic layer, giving the haiku a gentle cadence.
